0518, "title": "Michael Mann's 'Heat' Copyright Fight Turns on a Deal with Himself", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:00:00Z", "url": "https://copyrightlately.com/michael-mann-heat-copyright-termination/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Betelbuddy"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Just 400 US Data Centers Use More Electricity Than Michigan"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://www.wired.com/story/data-centers-use-more-electricity-than-michigan/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_Betelbuddy", "story_50520697", "front_page"], "author": "Betelbuddy", "children": [50520875, 50520980, 50520992, 50521052, 50521143, 50521279, 50521295], "created_at": "2026-11-16T18:04:55Z", "created_at_i": 1794852295, "num_comments": 16, "objectID": "50520697", "points": 18, "story_id": 50520697, "title": "Just 400 US Data Centers Use More Electricity Than Michigan", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T19:00:00Z", "url": "https://www.wired.com/story/data-centers-use-more-electricity-than-michigan/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "surprisetalk"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Quxnet Is a Breath of Fresh Air"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://moddedbear.com/quxnet-is-a-breath-of-fresh-air/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_surprisetalk", "story_50466300", "front_page"], "author": "surprisetalk", "children": [50468971, 50520994, 50521127, 50521243], "created_at": "2026-11-12T12:40:05Z", "created_at_i": 1794487205, "num_comments": 4, "objectID": "50466300", "points": 9, "story_id": 50466300, "title": "Quxnet Is a Breath of Fresh Air", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T18:55:30Z", "url": "https://moddedbear.com/quxnet-is-a-breath-of-fresh-air/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "tigranbs"}, "story_text": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Hi HN, I am Tigran (github.com/tigranbs)\nI made Fakemetrics.com as a fun experiment while testing how well Claude Opus can build pixel-identical UIs. It turned out it wasn't as easy as just prompting it, but I spent time building the system so it works almost every time.\nAnd I am pretty sure you are seeing a bunch of people posting weekend vibe-coded apps and saying &quot;$50K/month after quitting my McDonnalds job...&quot;. Well, even my friend tried to fake it a few months back.\nSo, I kinda did this fakemetrics.com as an experiment to see how well I can have the system that clones UIs, and packaged that as a very simple (I think) usable product for the people that want to be a superstar &quot;build in public&quot; type of a person with no revenue, but a perfect Stripe user growth screenshot.\nUseful? - Probably not that much\nFun? - YES!!\nThe best part is that Claude, ChatGPT, or Grok models aren't that good at UI clones by default, but with fakemetrics.com I kinda made a system that produces near-identical results from screenshots fairly fast. That was worth learning!\nLet me know what you think? Should I move on with the UI cloning as an open-source product?"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "Show HN: Fakemetrics.com – \"build in public\" like a superstar"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://fakemetrics.com/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_tigranbs", "story_50520741", "show_hn", "front_page"], "author": "tigranbs", "created_at": "2026-11-16T18:08:04Z", "created_at_i": 1794852484, "num_comments": 0, "objectID": "50520741", "points": 8, "story_id": 50520741, "story_text": "Hi HN, I am Tigran (github.com&#x2F;tigranbs)\nI made Fakemetrics.com as a fun experiment while testing how well Claude Opus can build pixel-identical UIs. It turned out it wasn&#x27;t as easy as just prompting it, but I spent time building the system so it works almost every time.\nAnd I am pretty sure you are seeing a bunch of people posting weekend vibe-coded apps and saying &quot;$50K&#x2F;month after quitting my McDonnalds job...&quot;. Well, even my friend tried to fake it a few months back.\nSo, I kinda did this fakemetrics.com as an experiment to see how well I can have the system that clones UIs, and packaged that as a very simple (I think) usable product for the people that want to be a superstar &quot;build in public&quot; type of a person with no revenue, but a perfect Stripe user growth screenshot.\nUseful? - Probably not that much\nFun? - YES!!\nThe best part is that Claude, ChatGPT, or Grok models aren&#x27;t that good at UI clones by default, but with fakemetrics.com I kinda made a system that produces near-identical results from screenshots fairly fast. That was worth learning!\nLet me know what you think? Should I move on with the UI cloning as an open-source product?", "title": "Show HN: Fakemetrics.com – \"build in public\" like a superstar", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T18:58:59Z", "url": "https://fakemetrics.com/"}, {"_highlightResult": {"author": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "ericzawo"}, "title": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "US Banks report outages in latest tech hiccup"}, "url": {"matchLevel": "none", "matchedWords": [], "value": "https://nypost.com/2026/11/16/business/outages-hit-chase-bank-of-america-and-wells-fargo-customers/"}}, "_tags": ["story", "author_ericzawo", "story_50521357", "front_page"], "author": "ericzawo", "created_at": "2026-11-16T18:53:00Z", "created_at_i": 1794855180, "num_comments": 0, "objectID": "50521357", "points": 5, "story_id": 50521357, "title": "US Banks report outages in latest tech hiccup", "updated_at": "2026-11-16T18:58:59Z", "url": "https://nypost.com/2026/11/16/business/outages-hit-chase-bank-of-america-and-wells-fargo-customers/"}], "hitsPerPage": 50, "nbHits": 30, "nbPages": 1, "page": 0, "params": "tags=front_page&hitsPerPage=50&advancedSyntax=true&analyticsTags=